Package: squall
Architecture: all
Depends:
 squall-gtk (= ${source:Version}),
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: lightweight, lean BitTorrent client (metapackage)
 Squall is a lightweight, lean BitTorrent client written in Python. It uses
 a client-server model supporting multiple user-interfaces that can connect
 to a (headless) daemon running on a server:
 .
   * squall-gtk: graphical UI using GTK
   * squall-console: text UI using ncurses
   * squall-web: web frontend
 .
 This package is a metapackage depending on the graphical UI and the
 daemon for running Squall on a single machine.

Package: squall-common
Architecture: all
Depends:
 python3-gi,
 python3-gi-cairo,
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: lightweight, lean BitTorrent client (common)
 Squall is a lightweight, lean BitTorrent client written in Python. It uses
 a client-server model supporting multiple user-interfaces that can connect
 to a (headless) squall-daemon running on a server.
 .
 This package contains the shared virtualenv and files between the clients
 and the server.

